{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>מתיך</b> Four times in the Masorah: three here, and one \"יְחַיּוּ מֵתֶיךָ.\" And the three here are defective, for one dead person is intended, whereas that one there is plene, for the plural is intended. And there is a hint here to what they said: \"מְתֵי אֶרֶץ יָשִׁיךְ\" — for here it is written \"יְחַיּוּ מֵתֶיךָ,\" there it is written \"יְחַיּוּ מֵתֵי מֵתֶיךָ\" — here: יְחַיּוּ מֵתֶיךָ, there: יְחַיּוּ מֵתֶיךָ." "<b>לא יכלה</b> Two times: here, and the other: \"בְּשֵׁבֶט עֶבְרָתוֹ יָכְלָה.\" Therefore \"לא יכלה ממך\" from burying your dead — for every person must fear death, and if he does not give him a burial place, he too will have no burial place."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {0 "The comment as transmitted appears to contain a garbled repetition of the phrase יחיו מתיך/מתיך; the final juxtaposition readings collapse into the same form. Translated hyper-literally as it stands. The phrase מתי ארץ ישיך is from Psalms 105:22."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:16:45.870179180Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}